<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't wants to reduce coffee stocks.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't wants to reduce coffee stocks.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government would like to see its 13.8 million 60-kg bag stockpile reduced to between five and six million bags, said the head of the primary commodities department of the Industry and Commerce Ministry.</p>
<p>&quot;The ideal thing would be for stocks to be 30 percent of internal consumption, around five to six million bags,&quot; Mauricio Assis told reporters after a meeting with soluble industry officials.</p>
<p>Assis did not say how or when the government planned to reduce its stockpile.</p>
<p>((-- Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485417))</p>
